Structuring of Arcade Game
1. Controllers for Player 1 and 2 - Have a class for this Player class
    - Inherits the turtle class (Multiple square turtles)
    - Single line that moves up and down with keys
2. Ball class 
    - Inherits the turtle class (No key controller is needed)
    - Ball starts from the middle
    - When the ball touches to the player stick it bounces back to the other side
3. Scoreboard class
    - Whoever send the ball to the empty part of the screen gets the point
4. Setting up the screen
    - Coordinates 
    - Two sides seperated with dashed line showing two players
